      "description": "Vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU PhD Studies For potential PhD students Vacant PhD positions PhD studies at Aarhus University For potential PhD students Why do a PhD at Aarhus University How to apply for a PhD programme Vacant PhD positions PhD programmes PhD fellowships and scholarships For current PhD students Contact Vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University The graduate schools at Aarhus University offer both predefined PhD projects and the option of applying with one’s own PhD project description through an open call. You will find deadlines and requirements for all types of PhD positions, fellowships and scholarships on the individual graduate school websites. The calls will be published at least two weeks prior to deadline. Read more below about Vacant PhD positions at Arts , Aarhus BSS , Health , Natural Sciences , Technical Sciences Graduate School - Faculty of Arts Programmes at Graduate School of Arts ­Anthropology, Global Studies and the Study of Religion Art, Literature and Cultural Studies Didactics History, Archaeology and Classical Studies ICT, Media, Communication and Journalism Language, Linguistics, Communication and Cognition Learning and Education Theology, History of Ideas and Philosophy Vacant positions - Faculty of Arts Aarhus BSS Graduate School Programmes at Aarhus BSS Graduate School Business Development and Technology Economics and Business Economics Law Management Political Science Psychology and Behavioral Science Vacant positions at Aarhus BSS Graduate School Graduate School of Health Programmes at Graduate School og Health Biomedicine Public Health ClinFO (Clinical Medicine, Odontology and Forensic Medicine) Vacant positions at Graduate School of Health Graduate School of Natural Sciences Programmes at Graduate School of Natural Sciences Biology Chemistry Computer Science Geoscience Mathematics Molecular Biology and Genetics Nanoscience Physics and Astronomy Vacant positions at Graduate School of Natural Sciences Graduate School of Technical Sciences Programmes at Graduate School of Technical Sciences Agroecology Animal Science Bioscience Biological and Chemical Engineering Civil and Architectural Engineering Ecoscience Electrical and Computer Engineering Environmental Sciences Food Science Mechanical and Production Engineering Quantitative Genetics and Genomics Vacant positions at Graduate School of Technical Sciences Fellowships and scholarships for PhD students Read more about the different types of fellowships and scholarships offered by Aarhus University. Revised\n    24.08.2026 - AU PhD and Fond Services Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: au@au.dk Tel: +45 8715 0000 Fax: +45 8715 0201 CVR no: 31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 17495 / i43 English Danish Cookies improve user experience When you click 'Accept all' cookies, Aarhus University can give you the best user experience. Cookies store information about how a user interacts with a website. All your data is anonymised and cannot be used to identify you. You can always change your consent again under ‘Cookies' in the website footer. The university uses its own cookies and cookies set by our partners. Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified Save & Close Accept all Decline all Read more about cookies Hide details List of cookies Cookie Policy Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified These cookies make it possible to use basic website functionality, e.g. navigation etc. The website does not work without t