unt of time of your visit to the website, what pages you have visited, whether your computer, tablet or smartphone has used the pages before, which website you came from, which browser and operating system you use and the like. In some cases, IP addresses are also collected, which are personally identifiable data. Therefore, you can also read our Privacy Policy , which tells how we at AU process personal information. If any of the third party services, we use, process data on behalf of AU, we will, if possible, enter into a Data Processing Agreement with them. The supplier is thus not allowed to use the data for their own purposes or to pass them on to others. Delete cookies It is also possible to delete or block cookies. See the guide: https://www.allaboutcookies.org/manage-cookies/clear-cookies-installed.html The website is owned and published by: Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 DK-8000 Aarhus C Tel. no: 87 15 00 00 Email: au@au.dk Cookies consent ID : Cookie report created by CookieScript"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/index.php?id=147606": {
      "title": "Future and career",
      "description": "Future and career Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU Danish website You are here: AU Life in Denmark For students Future and career Life in Denmark Danish way of living Your new city For students Prepare your arrival International Students Guide Housing Student Life AU Green Guide Future and career Career perspectives Extending your stay Leaving Denmark For PhDs and researchers Future and career To prepare you for the future and your first job after graduation, Aarhus University offers comprehensive career services for all international students. As an international student, you are invited to participate in various workshops and events that will prepare you for working in Denmark. Skills training Wondering how you can write an effective CV or cover letter? Or how you can use LinkedIn to find a job? At Aarhus University you can attend workshops and sessions and receive practical skills training throughout your studies. Skills Training: CV, Cover Letter and LinkedIn Learning Danish Knowing just a bit of Danish can make a big difference – both in your social life and when you look for work. To make learning Danish as easy as possible, you can join classes right on campus. Learning Danish: Danish work culture, Danish classes and Danish job market Networking Every semester you can attend job fairs and networking events on campus. This is your opportunity to meet local companies and employers and also to meet and get inspired by international graduates from your field. Networking: Job Fairs, Networking with graduates and AU job portal Meet the Career service centres at AU How do I find the first job? What makes you qualified? How do you write a CV or a motivation letter? Get in contact with our Career Service Centre at your faculty, attend some of our workshops and get advice on a more personal level. Aarhus BSS ARTS Natural and Technical Sciences Meet the graduates The Danish labour market is known for high job mobility, flexibility and high-quality working conditions. Many international AU students decide to stay and work in Denmark after graduation due to the work-life balance. Career perspectives Learn more about working in Denmark AU Alumni network Meet Vladislava Garkova Vladislava Garkova landed her first job soon after graduating. Actually, she landed the job quicker than she had expected herself. By gaining experience while studying, establishing a solid network, and being open to many opportunities, she made herself an attractive candidate to companies. Meet Wilson from Vestas, a wind turbine production company Originally from Brazil, Wilson was drawn to Denmark by its reputation for promoting sustainability. He studied Biotechnology and Chemical Engineering with a specialization in Environmental Technologies at Aarhus University, and now works for Vestas while living in Ringkøbing, Denmark. Chat with AU alumni Meet other International students - come socialize with us a StudenterhusAarhus! Join us for a hygge time; meet new friends and try new activities. We offer the opportunity to learn something new, grow your network and feel at home which is important during your studies as well as after graduation when staying in Denmark. Want to know more about StudenterhusAarhus? Come socialize with us! Do you have an idea for a startup? Would like to get some support to develop it further? The Kitchen is a public workspace and café open to everyone. But above all it is Aarhus University’s startup hub! Whether you’re a student, PhD or researcher The Kitchen aims to help you make informed decisions and match you with the resources you need to grow.  We have a range of programs and courses tailored the different stages of your entrepreneurial journey. Come meet us at the Kitchen! Revised\n    26.06.2026 - International Centre Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: au@au.dk Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 147606 / i48 English Danish Cookies improve user experience When you click 'Accept all' cookies, Aarhus University can give you the best user experience. Cookies store information about how a user interacts with a website. All your data is anonymised and cannot be used to identify you. You can always change your consent again under ‘Cookies' in the website footer. The university uses its own cookies and cookies set by our partners. Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified Save & Close Accept all Decline all Read more about cookies Hide details List of cookies Cookie Policy Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified These cookies make it possible to use basic website functionality, e.g. navigation etc. The website does not work without these cookies. Cookie report Name Provider / Domain Expires Description be_typo_user TYPO3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is set by our CMS provider; TYPO3 and is used to identify a backend session when a Backend User is logged in to TYPO3 Backend or Frontend. fe_typo_user Typo3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is associated with the Typo3 web content management system. It is generally used as a user session identifier to enable user preferences to be stored, but in many cases it may not actually be needed as it can be set by default by the platform, though this can be prevented by site administrators. In most cases it is set to be destroyed at the end of a browser session. It contains a random identifier rather than any specific user data. ASP.NET_SessionId Microsoft Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform sessi