    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/innovation-positions-associate-professor-professor-at-aarhus-university-faculty-of-technical-sciences": {
      "title": "Innovation Positions (Associate Professor / Professor)",
      "description": "Innovation Positions (Associate Professor / Professor) at Aarhus University – Faculty of Technical Sciences - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU Danish website You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability Campus development History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Technical Sciences Innovation Positions (Associate Professor / Professor) at Aarhus University – Faculty of Technical Sciences Deadline 10 Sep 23:59 CEST Expected start 1 Apr Technical Sciences Ny Munkegade 120 8000 Aarhus C Full-time position ID: 164834 Apply ATTENTION: Contact persons are listed in the background document, which can be accessed here . __________________________________________________________________________________________________ Aarhus University is currently expanding its strategic efforts within innovation and entrepreneurship, with the aim of bringing more research into play as concrete societal solutions, spin-outs, and collaborations with established companies. This initiative is closely aligned with Aarhus University’s Strategy 2030, where research-based innovation and entrepreneurship constitute a central strategic focus area. With the aim of expanding Aarhus University’s capacity to bridge research and innovation, the university leadership has decided to establish a number of strategic new research and innovation positions across the university. These positions are intended to contribute to integrating innovation thinking into the university’s culture while at the same time ensuring tangible impact and societal value. Expected date of accession: April 1st 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. The positions The Faculty of Technical Sciences (Tech) invites applications for a number of positions at Associate Professor or Professor level within innovation-focused research and impact across its departments and in the areas of food systems, environment and engineering. Positions may be offered as full-time academic appointments or as joint appointments with industry or public sector partners, depending on the candidates profile. Candidates are expected to contribute to building the link between research, innovation, and society, and to engage and strengthen the collaboration across departments and across Aarhus University with respect to interdisciplinary innovation efforts. Due to the breadth of the call, applicants will be evaluated by an assessment committee with knowledge tailored to the thematic areas of relevance. Thematic areas The specific themes are presented below and elaborated in a memo which can be found here . Applicants must clearly state in their application i) which of the  the following thematic areas they are applying to, and ii) which level the candidate is applying for (Associate Professor / Professor): Theme 1: Innovation Hub for Feed and Food Processing hosted by the Department of Animal  and Veterinary Science Theme 2: Resilient crops with new genomic techniques (NGT) hosted by the Department of Agroecology Theme 3: Integrating nature-based/technical solutions to address multiple water challenges at catchment scales Theme 4: Bioaerosol surveillance and integrated early warning systems hosted by The Department of Environmental Science Theme 5: Food biosolutions and hybrid food systems hosted by The Department of Food Science Theme 6: Digital phenotyping across plants, insects and farmed animals hosted by the Centre for Quantitative Genetics and Genomics. Theme 7: Water technology hosted by the Department of Biological and Chemical Engineering Theme 8: Advanced production technologies for biogenic building materials hosted by the Department of Civil and Architectural Engineering Theme 9: Building the resilient, flexible, multi-energy microgrids of tomorrow hosted by the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering Theme 10: Advanced Materials, Biomechanical Systems, Human-centric and Intelligent Manufacturing for a Sustainable and Resilient society hosted by the Department of Mechanical and Production Engineering Responsibilities Selected candidates are expected to: Conduct high-quality research with a clear innovation and impact orientation Contribute to the translation of research into practical and societally relevant applications Establish and expand collaborations with industry and other innovation hubs, public sector organisations, including external partners outside AU Engage in interdisciplinary collaboration across departments and faculties Contribute to teaching, supervision, and mentorship of students and early-career researchers Strengthen innovation capacity within the department and the broader faculty Qualifications and evaluation criteria Applicants will be assessed based on both traditional academic criteria (academic excellence, research portfolio, and teaching / dissemination experience) and additional innovation-related criteria. In particular, emphasis will be placed on: The innovation potential of the applicant’s field of expertise A clear vision and plan for innovation activities (to be described in the application or as a separate document) Demonstrated or potential societal impact within a relatively short time horizon Documented experience and skills within innovation, including concrete examples Relevant academic qualifications relevant to the selected thematic area Experience with collaboration with external partners All candidates will also be assessed in relation to departmental priorities within the thematic area. What we offer A well-established and supportive, interdisciplinary and internationally recognised research environment Close interaction with industry and public sector partners Access to advanced research infrastructure and innovation ecosystems Opportunities to shape and develop innovation capacity across Tech and AU Organisation and place of work The place of employment is Aarhus University, Faculty of Technical Sciences. The positions will be anchored in the departments mentioned under each theme. Tech have activities in Aarhus, Roskilde, Flakkebjerg, Viborg and Herning. The place of work will be determined on the candidate’s qualifications, the relevant department’s geographical presence, its priorities and opportunities, and personal preferences. Candidates are expected to engage broadly across the faculty and contribute to cross-cutting innovation initiatives. Contact information If you have any questions about the position, then please contact the relevant person responsible for the area you are interested in. The relevant contact person can be found here . Application deadline Applications must be received no later than 10 September 2026. Application procedure Applications must be submitted in English and include: Curriculum vitae List of publications Description of research and innovation activities A statement outlining the candidate’s vision for innovation Teaching and supervision portfolio (e.g.  including dissemination, communicaiton, mentorship) Guidelines for applicants can be found here. Shortlisting is used. This means that after the deadline for applications – and with the assistance from the assessment committee chairman, and the assessment committee if necessary, – the head of department selects the candidates to be evaluated. The selection is made on the basis of an assessment of who of the candidates are most relevant considering the requirements of the advertisement. All applicants will be notified within 6 weeks whether or not their applications have been sent to an expert assessment committee for evaluation. The selected applicants will be informed about the composition of the committee and will receive his/her assessment. Formalities and salary range Appointment shall be in accordance with the collective labour agreement between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations. Further information on qualification requirements and job content may be found in the Memorandum on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Danish Universities. Salary depends on seniority as agreed between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Confederation of Professional Associations. You will be appointed as professor or associate professor. Appointment as associate professor follows the basic salary steps 4-8 according to the collective agreement for academics employed by the state. The employment includes a pensionable pay supplement of DKK 91,282.00 per year at 31.03.2012 level in connection with full-time employment. Professors are paid a salary corresponding to salary step 37 according to Circular on the Protocol on Certain Terms and Conditions of Employment for Academic Staff at Universities. The employment includes a pensionable pay supplement of DKK 51,400.00 per year at 31.03.2012 level in connection with full-time employment. Your salary consists of a basic salary and a pensionable pay supplement and possibly an individually negotiated qualifications supplement. Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. Research activities will be evaluated in relation to actual research time. Thus, we encourage applicants to specify periods of leave without research activities, in order to be able to subtract these periods from the span of the scientific career during the evaluation of scientific productivity. Aarhus University offers a broad variety of services for international researchers and accompanying families, including relocation service and career counselling to expat partners. Read more here . Please find more information about entering and working in Denmark here . The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Michelle H. Williams Vice-Dean, Dean's Office, Technical Sciences +4525170049 mhw@au.dk Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Nat-Tech Administrative Centre - Nat-Tech HR +4593521026 nat-tech.HR.team2@au.dk Apply Deadline: \n                            Thursday 10 Sep 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: au@au.dk Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48 English Danish Cookies improve user experience When you click 'Accept all' cookies, Aarhus University can give you the best user experience. Cookies store information about how a user interacts with a website. All your data is anonymised and cannot be used to identify you. You can always change your consent again under ‘Cookies' in the website footer. The university uses its own cookies and cookies set by our partners. Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified Save & Close Accept all Decline all Read more about cookies Hide details List of cookies Cookie Policy Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified These cookies make it possible to use basic website functionality, e.g. navigation etc. The website does not work without these cookies. Cookie report Name Provider / Domain Expires Description be_typo_user TYPO3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is set by our CMS provider; TYPO3 and is used to identify a backend session when a Backend User is logged in to TYPO3 Backend or Frontend. fe_typo_user Typo3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is associated with the Typo3 web content management system. It is generally used as a user session identifier to enable user preferences to be stored, but in many cases it may not actually be needed as it can be set by default by the platform, though this can be prevented by site administrators. In most cases it is set to be destroyed at the end of a browser session. It contains a random identifier rather than any specific user data. ASP.NET_SessionId Microsoft Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written with Miscrosoft .NET based technologies. Usually used to maintain an anonymised user session by the server. JSESSIONID Oracle Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written in JSP. Usually used to maintain an anonymous user session by the server. ARRAffinity Microsoft Corporation .mitstudie.au.dk Session This cookie is set by websites run on the Windows Azure cloud platform. It is used for load balancing to make sure the visitor page requests are routed to the same server in any browsing session. esctx Microsoft Corporation .login.microsoftonline.com Session This cookie is used by Microsoft to securely verify your login information fpc Microsoft Corporation login.microsoftonline.com 4 weeks 2 days This 