ain. What data is collected via cookies? Most cookies collect anonymous data, such as the amount of time of your visit to the website, what pages you have visited, whether your computer, tablet or smartphone has used the pages before, which website you came from, which browser and operating system you use and the like. In some cases, IP addresses are also collected, which are personally identifiable data. Therefore, you can also read our Privacy Policy , which tells how we at AU process personal information. If any of the third party services, we use, process data on behalf of AU, we will, if possible, enter into a Data Processing Agreement with them. The supplier is thus not allowed to use the data for their own purposes or to pass them on to others. Delete cookies It is also possible to delete or block cookies. See the guide: https://www.allaboutcookies.org/manage-cookies/clear-cookies-installed.html The website is owned and published by: Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 DK-8000 Aarhus C Tel. no: 87 15 00 00 Email: au@au.dk Cookies consent ID : Cookie report created by CookieScript"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/rengoeringsassistent-sanitoer-19": {
      "title": "Rengøringsassistent/Sanitør",
      "description": "Rengøringsassistent/Sanitør  - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU Danish website You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability Campus development History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Health Administrative Centre - Health Byg Rengøring Rengøringsassistent/Sanitør Deadline 11 Sep 23:59 CEST Expected start 1 Nov Health Administrative Centre - Health Byg Rengøring Vennelyst Boulevard 9 8000 Aarhus C Part-time position 20 hours per week ID: 167878 Apply Trives du i rollen som rengøringsassistent/sanitør, har vi 1 ledige stillinger, som afløser på 20 timer pr. uge inden for rengøringsområdet på Health Sciences, Aarhus Universitet. Med opstart den 1. november 2026. Du bliver en del af rengøringsområdet i bygningsservice. I bygningsservice på Health er vi 45 kolleger, hvoraf 43 er tilknyttet rengøringsområdet. Bygningsservice varetager den daglige vedligeholdelse, drift og servicering af bygningsmassen. Health råder over ca. 90.000 kvadratmeter forsknings-og uddannelsesbygninger med nogle af landets mest avancerede laboratorier, eksperimentelle anlæg og forskningsfaciliteter. Vi har et åbent arbejdsmiljø, hvor vi lægger vægt på ansvarlighed, engagement og plads til den enkelte. Dine arbejdsopgaver Som rengøringsassistent/sanitør er dine primære arbejdsopgaver rengøring af auditorier, laboratorier, øvrige undervisningslokaler, kontorer og toiletter. Vi arbejder ud fra konkrete rengøringsplaner i de forskellige områder af fakultetet. Du refererer til Rengøringsleder Joan Warthoe. Dine kompetencer Vi forestiller os, at du har flair for og lyst til at gøre rent. Vi lægger vægt på, at du er stabil og engageret i dit arbejde. Som person er du positiv, imødekommende og har let ved at opbygge tillidsfulde relationer, men kan også blive stående i modvind. Du har et stort drive, du byder ind i forhold til opgaver og evner at prioritere dine opgaver. Du skal kunne tale og skrive dansk og meget gerne have erfaring med rengøring. Spørgsmål til stillingen Har du spørgsmål til stillingen, er du velkommen til at kontakte Rengøringsleder Joan Warthoe. Joan Warthoe kan kontaktes mellem kl. 9 – 11 på hverdage på tlf.: +45 9350 8660. Arbejdsstedet er Healths bygninger i Universitetsparken, 8000 Aarhus C Arbejdstiden er mandag til fredag fra kl. 05.00 Der ydes ulempetillæg for arbejdstid før kl. 06.00 Ansættelsesgrundlag Løn- og ansættelsesvilkår sker i henhold til organisationsaftalen for rengøringsassistenter, sanitører, specialarbejdere og visse erhvervsuddannede m.fl. i staten m.v. (3F) og fællesoverenskomsten mellem Finansministeriet og Offentligt Ansattes Organisationer – Det statslige Område (OAO-S-fællesoverenskomsten). Ansøgning Din ansøgning skal indeholde følgende: Ansøgning Curriculum Vitae Angivelse af uddannelse (kopi af relevante eksamensbeviser) Referencer/anbefalinger kan uploades særskilt i e-rekrutteringssystemet Vi henviser til fakultetets Vejledning for ansøgere . Aarhus Universitet vil være en attraktiv og inspirerende arbejdsplads for alle og ønsker en kultur, hvor hver enkelt kan udfolde og udvikle sig. Vi ser ligestilling og diversitet som en ressource og opfordrer derfor alle interesserede til at ansøge. Ansøgning sendes via Aarhus Universitets rekrutteringssystem, som kan tilgås under stillingsopslaget på Aarhus Universitets hjemmeside. Questions about the position\n                            ? Joan Warthoe Cleaning Manager, Health Administrative Centre - Health Byg Rengøring +4593508660 joanwarthoe@au.dk Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Health Administrative Centre - Health HR +4593521539 emply.he.hr@au.dk Apply Deadline: \n                            Friday 11 Sep 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: au@au.dk Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48 English Danish Cookies improve user experience When you click 'Accept all' cookies, Aarhus University can give you the best user experience. Cookies store information about how a user interacts with a website. All your data is anonymised and cannot be used to identify you. You can always change your consent again under ‘Cookies' in the website footer. The university uses its own cookies and cookies set by our partners. Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified Save & Close Accept all Decline all Read more about cookies Hide details List of cookies Cookie Policy Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified These cookies make it possible to use basic website functionality, e.g. navigation etc. The website does not work without these cookies. Cookie report Name Provider / Domain Expires Description be_typo_user TYPO3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is set by our CMS provider; TYPO3 and is used to identify a backend session when a Backend User is logged in to TYPO3 Backend or Frontend. fe_typo_user Typo3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is associated with the Typo3 web content management system. It is generally used as a user session identifier to enable user preferences to be stored, but in many cases it may not actually be needed as it can be set by default by the platform, though this can be prevented by site administrators. In most cases it is set to be destroyed at the end of a browser session. It contains a random identifier rather than any specific user data. ASP.NET_SessionId Microsoft Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written with Miscrosoft .NET based technologies. Usually used to maintain an anonymised user session by the server. JSESSIONID Oracle Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written in JSP. Usually used to maintain an anonymous user session by the server. ARRAffinity Microsoft Corporation .mitstudie.au.dk Session This cookie is set by websites run on the Windows Azure cloud platform. It is used for load balancing to make sure the visitor page requests are routed to the same server in any browsing session. esctx Microsoft Corporation .login.microsoftonline.com Session This cookie is used by Microsoft to securely verify your login information fpc Microsoft Corporation login.microsoftonline.com 4 weeks 2 days This cookie is used by Microsoft to securely verify your login information __cf_bm Cloudflare Inc. .pure.au.dk 29 minutes 59 seconds This cookie is used to distinguish between humans and bots. This is beneficial for the website, in order to make valid reports on the use of their website. __Secure-typo3nonce_ouB7_tePaslDY7zpIHG6wg aias.au.dk Session __cf_bm Cloudflare Inc. .linkedin.com 29 minutes 59 seconds This cookie is used to distinguish between humans and bots. This is beneficial for the website, in order to make valid reports on the use of their website. __cf_bm Cloudflare Inc. .twitter.com 29 minutes 5