    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/associate-professor-in-inclusive-teaching-practice-in-higher-education-at-the-centre-for-educational-development": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in Inclusive Teaching Practice in Higher Education",
      "description": "Associate Professor in Inclusive Teaching Practice in Higher Education at the Centre for Educational Development - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU Danish website You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability Campus development History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Teaching Development Associate Professor in Inclusive Teaching Practice in Higher Education at the Centre for Educational Development Deadline 13 Sep 23:59 CEST Expected start 1 Feb Teaching Development Trøjborgvej 82-84 8000 Aarhus C Full-time position ID: 165626 Apply We invite applications for an associate professorship focusing on inclusive classroom collaboration and teaching that fosters student engagement in the higher education (university) setting. About this position The position calls for creative, interdisciplinary scholars able to bridge empirical and philosophical traditions within the learning sciences. We expect you to have a deep understanding of the underlying cognitive mechanisms, as well as the experiential conditions supporting motivation and engagement. We are looking for a colleague working with topics like universal design, inclusivity, belonging, accessibility, transformative pedagogy, collaborative learning, difficult university classroom conversations or conflicts, student engagement, and motivation in higher education. At CED, an associate professor’s time divides equally between research and teaching. We expect you to contribute to CED´s research environment, while taking an active role in our university teacher training program and the development of innovative pedagogical approaches across AU. We expect you to be passionate about translating research into educational practice. About your expected tasks and responsibilities Your primary tasks and responsibilities as an associate professor at CED are to Conduct internationally recognized applied research on inclusive teaching in higher education Publish and communicate your research internationally and in relevant Danish contexts Fundraise externally for research activities at CED Supervise younger researchers in relevant focus areas Lead teaching development projects within your field of expertise Collaborate with academic communities at AU to create experiments and innovate teaching Teach broader (selected) topics at CED’s courses and workshops for AU staff/faculty, including taking on responsibilities of course management and coordination Support colleagues at CED in connection with other tasks by specific agreement. About your qualifications and competence You have A PhD degree in a relevant field At least three years of postdoc or assistant professor work-experience in a relevant position (at time of application) Developed a relevant, independent, international research profile, that includes topics like universal design, transformative pedagogy, student engagement, motivation, inclusion, experiential learning, embodied cognition, conflict, collaborative learning, belonging Successful fundraising experience Broad teaching experience, including experience of teaching university staff/faculty Obtained a teaching certificate / pedagogical course certificate from your previous postdoc or assistant professor period Practical experience leading development projects within your field of expertise. You are ready to Supervise younger research colleagues Collaborate respectfully and professionally with university staff and faculty across AU and with colleagues at CED with quite different educational backgrounds and tasks Be present at Aarhus University most days Learn Danish (if you are not already speaking a Scandinavian language) You are a person who Thrives on complex processes with multiple agendas and stakeholders Have strategies for coping with projects that are necessarily going as planned. About the Centre for Educational Development (CED) at Aarhus University (AU) CED is the educational development and teaching-learning centre at AU. The mission of CED is to inspire engaging teaching and excellent educations at Aarhus University. We offer all faculties, staff, and educational leaders at AU courses and workshops, practical partnership, and collaboration about their students, their teaching, their curricula and programs, to foster and assist the implementation of research-based educational development. We also run, support, develop, and inspire the use of learning technologies at AU. CED employs about 60 colleagues organized into three departments specialized in digital development, teaching development, and program development, respectively, plus a small administration. We have a good collegial atmosphere characterized by a high degree of collaboration and continuous professional development. We value inquiry, co-creation, empowerment, and expertise. The research group at CED works within and across the three departments. The group presently comprises six associate professors, four assistant professors, two postdocs, five PhD-students and three research assistants. The group has ongoing research on topics that include student learning, transitions and career, university teacher development and educational leadership, health sciences education, natural sciences education, and learning technologies in higher education. We come from a wide range of research methods and theoretical frameworks, but all focus on applied higher education research. For a more detailed description of CED, please, visit our website. Conditions and place of employment The position is full time (37 hours per week). Expected start date 1 February 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. Further information on the appointment procedure can be found in the Ministerial Orde r on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities . The appointment is in accordance with the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations (Akademikerne). Further information on qualification requirements and job description can be found in the Ministerial Order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities. The successful applicant will refer to the department manager of Teaching Development at CED. The Centre director lead the research group across the three departments. Place of employment is Trøjborgvej 82-84, 8000 Aarhus C, Denmark. International applicant? Aarhus University offers a broad variety of services for international researchers and accompanying families, including relocation service and career counselling to expat partners. Please find more information about entering and working in Denmark on Research at AU. The hiring process In connection with your motivated written application, you must also attach CV Documentation for your PhD degree List of all your publications Three selected full publications for deep assessment A research plan covering the first two years at CED as an associate professor (max 3 pages) Description of your fundraising successes (1 page) Your teaching portfolio (max 3 pages) A short teaching statement (or teaching philosophy) Documentation of participation in university teaching courses And examples of leading educational development projects (max 3 pages). Applications must be made in English. We use shortlisting in the hiring process lead by the centre director. In the shortlisting process, we exclude applicants that are far from being eligible for the described position. After the shortlisting process, an assessment committee with international participation gives their written summary concerning each of the shortlisted applicants. Based on these summaries of qualifications, an employment committee of future colleagues from CED invite the best 3-4 applicants for an interview. Interviews are expected to take place in December. Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Anne Mette Mørcke Centre Director, Centre for Educational Development - CED +4551447574 morcke@au.dk Questions about application and proces\n                            ? AU HR - Employment Law +4529454108 emply.fa.hr@au.dk Apply Deadline: \n                            Sunday 13 Sep 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: au@au.dk Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48 English Danish Cookies improve user experience When you click 'Accept all' cookies, Aarhus University can give you the best user experience. Cookies store information about how a user interacts with a website. All your data is anonymised and cannot be used to identify you. You can always change your consent again under ‘Cookies' in the website footer. The university uses its own cookies and cookies set by our partners. Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified Save & Close Accept all Decline all Read more about cookies Hide details List of cookies Cookie Policy Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified These cookies make it possible to use basic website functionality, e.g. navigation etc. The website does not work without these cookies. Cookie report Name Provider / Domain Expires Description be_typo_user TYPO3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is set by our CMS provider; TYPO3 and is used to identify a backend session when a Backend User is logged in to TYPO3 Backend or Frontend. fe_typo_user Typo3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is associated with the Typo3 web content management system. It is generally used as a user session identifier to enable user preferences to be stored, but in many cases it may not actually be needed as it can be set by default by the platform, though this can be prevented by site administrators. In most cases it is set to be destroyed at the end of a browser session. It contains a random identifier rather than any specific user data. ASP.NET_SessionId Microsoft Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written with Miscrosoft .NET based technologies. Usually used to maintain an anonymised user session by the server. JSESSIONID Oracle Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written in JSP. Usually used to maintain an anonymous user session by the server. ARRAffinity Microsoft Corporation .mitstudie.au.dk Session This cookie is set by websites run on the Windows Azure cloud platform. It is used for load balancing to make sure the visitor page requests are routed to the same server in any browsing session. esctx Microsoft Corpor