    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/professor-associate-professor-senior-researcher-taking-lead-in-arctic-environment-and-ecosystem-sciences": {
      "title": "Professor / Associate Professor / Senior Researcher taking lead in Arctic environment and ecosystem sciences",
      "description": "Professor / Associate Professor / Senior Researcher taking lead in Arctic environment and ecosystem sciences - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU Danish website You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability Campus development History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Ecoscience - Faculty: Technical Sciences Professor / Associate Professor / Senior Researcher taking lead in Arctic environment and ecosystem sciences Deadline 13 Sep 23:59 CEST Expected start 1 Nov Department of Ecoscience Frederiksborgvej 399 4000 Roskilde Full-time position ID: 167058 Apply Are you an engaged and visionary scientist with international standing, deep expertise in Arctic environmental and ecosystem research and excellent science leadership competences? Do you have the scientific vision to set the strategic direction for a nationally and internationally recognized Arctic research community? The Department of Ecoscience at Aarhus University invites applications for a full-time permanent scientific position as either Full Professor, Associate Professor or Senior Researcher in the Arctic focus area. We are looking for a successful science leader who enjoys working strategically with organizational impact also looking beyond own research area. Expected start date and duration of employment This is a permanent position from 1 November 2026 or as soon as possible. Job description The position centers around research in Arctic terrestrial and/or marine environment and ecosystems, with expertise in one or more of the key thematic areas of the Arctic focus area, f.ex.: Arctic ecosystem responses to climate change and anthropogenic disturbance including natural resource exploitation like mining and other industrial activities, biodiversity and population ecology, biogeochemistry and carbon dynamics or environmental contaminants and ecotoxicology. Technical environmental and innovative solutions to current and future Arctic and global challenges Bridging monitoring and front-edge research within Arctic environment and ecosystem sciences Your primary scientific responsibilities may include: Taking lead on strategic development of central parts of the Arctic focus area Securing externally funded research projects, including EU research and innovation programmes and other national and international funding sources Bridging science and advice to agencies in Greenland and Denmark, as well as to relevant international fora, including within Arctic Council, particularly CAFF, AMAP and PAME. Conducting independent and leading research in Arctic ecosystems, biodiversity, environment and pollution, including drawing on long-term monitoring datasets, multidisciplinary field campaigns, and/or advanced modelling approaches Publishing in high-impact, peer-reviewed international journals and engaging actively with the international scientific community Supervising and mentoring PhD students, postdocs, and early-career researchers Depending on the candidate’s area of expertise, responsibilities may also include: Contributing to pan-Arctic comparative studies and to positioning ECOS Arctic in major international initiatives Driving forward the Departments engagement and steering of national initiatives (e.g. the International Polar Year 2032-33) Integrating novel tools and methods into research and advice to Greenlandic and Danish authorities, including AI-driven data analysis, process-based modelling, and ecological forecasting Your profile We are looking for a scientist with a strong research track record and documented experience with science based advisory work and expertise in Arctic ecosystem and environmental related science showing interdisciplinary and broad sectoral collaborative and leadership skills. Applicants must hold a PhD in biology, ecology, biogeochemistry, ecotoxicology, physical geography or a closely related discipline. The level of appointment (Full Professor, Associate Professor or Senior Researcher) will be determined based on qualifications. We particularly value: Excellent science leadership experience from similar research environments; f.ex. leading larger research groups and taking responsibility for strategic development of larger units (academic citizenship) An established international network and collaborative skills and relationships within Arctic science Competences in strategic scientific coordination, project management, and building research networks A strong publication record in international peer-reviewed journals within Arctic research Documented experience in securing and leading externally funded research projects Experience with fieldwork and/or laboratory analyses in Arctic environments Experience from Greenland institutions, collaboration or research Documented experience with science-based advisory work and engagement with authorities Experience in supervising and supporting early-career researchers Excellent written and spoken English; Danish and/or Greenlandic language skills are an advantage but not required Who we are The Department of Ecoscience is one of Denmark’s leading research environments in applied ecology, spanning terrestrial, freshwater, marine, and Arctic ecosystems. We conduct both fundamental and applied research and deliver science-based advisory services to authorities in Denmark and Greenland. Our work is grounded in long-term monitoring, field-based data collection, and advanced modelling, and we pride ourselves on a research culture characterized by high scientific integrity, strong interdisciplinary collaboration, and societal relevance. ECOS Arctic is the department’s Arctic focus area and an internationally recognized hub for Arctic ecosystem research and science-based advisory work, with excellence in ecology, biodiversity, biogeochemistry, environmental contaminants, and ecotoxicology. We are around 50 research and technical employees with Greenland as our primary base for Arctic science activities, and we are strongly anchored in the Greenland Ecosystem Monitoring (GEM) programme and to research and advise related to industrial (incl. mining) activities. But we also hold leading roles in Arctic Council working groups and contribute to pan-Arctic comparative research and global science initiatives. Key infrastructure supporting ECOS Arctic includes Zackenberg Research Station in Northeast Greenland and the accredited ECOS Trace Metal and Isotope Geochemistry Laboratory. Find out more about our current strategy, departmental values and more here: https://ecos.au.dk/en/about-us/au-ecoscience-our-strategy What we offer A full-time permanent scientific position with an internationally competitive research environment and access to unique long-term datasets and world-class infrastructure A central role in shaping the scientific direction of ECOS Arctic, contributing actively to the strategy 2026–2030 and beyond An interdisciplinary and dynamic working environment across Arctic, terrestrial, marine, and freshwater research Highly engaged, motivated and positive colleagues and an innovative and dynamic working environment, where culture and values are important. A working environment characterized by high scientific standards, trust, and well-being Strong international collaborative relationships and active participation in global Arctic research initiatives, including a leading role in preparation for the International Polar Year 2032 Access to professional support for international researchers and their families relocating to Denmark For candidates with the right qualifications and experience in strategic research leadership a temporary role as Deputy Head of Department with responsibility for the Arctic focus area of Department of Ecoscience will be possible. Further education/competence building in leadership will be offered. Contact the Head of Department (details below) for a more detailed description of this role. Place of work and area of employment The place of work is AU Campus Roskilde at Frederiksborgvej 399, DK-4000 Roskilde, Denmark, and the area of employment is Aarhus University with related departments. Deadline Applications must be received no later than 13 September 2026. Application procedure Shortlisting is used. This means that after the deadline for applications – and with the assistance from the assessment committee chairman, and the assessment committee if necessary, – the head of department selects the candidates to be evaluated. The selection is made on the basis of an assessment of who of the candidates are most relevant considering the requirements of the advertisement. All applicants will be notified within 6 weeks whether or not their applications have been sent to an expert assessment committee for evaluation. The selected applicants will be informed about the composition of the committee and will receive his/her assessment. Formalities and salary range Technical Sciences refers to the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Danish Universities under the Danish Ministry of Science, Technology and Innovation . The application must be in English and include a curriculum vitae, degree certificate, a complete list of publications, a statement of future research plans and information about research activities, teaching portfolio and verified information on previous teaching experience (if any). Guidelines for applicants can be found here. Appointment shall be in accordance with the collective labour agreement between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations. Further information on qualification requirements and job content may be found in the Memorandum on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Danish Universities. Salary and terms as agreed between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Confederation of Professional Unions at basic salary steps 4-8. Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. Research activities will be evaluated in relation to actual research time. Thus, we encourage applicants to specify periods of leave without research activities, in order to be able to subtract these periods from the span of the scientific career during the evaluation of scientific productivity. Aarhus University offers a broad variety of services for international researchers and accompanying families, including relocation service and career counselling to expat partners. Read more here . Please find more information about entering and working in Denmark here . The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Mikkel Tamstorf Head of Department, Department of Ecoscience - ECOS Roskilde +4553575044 mpt@ecos.au.dk Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Nat-Tech Administrative Centre - Nat-Tech HR +4593521026 nat-tech.HR.team2@au.dk Apply Deadline: \n                            Sunday 13 Sep 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: au@au.dk Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48 English Danish Cookies improve user experience When you click 'Accept all' cookies, Aarhus University can give you the best user experience. Cookies store information about how a user interacts with a website. All your data is anonymised and cannot be used to identify you. You can always change your consent again under ‘Cookies' in the website footer. The university uses its own cookies and cookies set by our partners. Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified Save & Close Accept all Decline all Read more about cookies Hide details List of cookies Cookie Policy Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified These cookies make it possible to use basic website functionality, e.g. navigation etc. The website does not work without these cookies. Cookie report Name Provider / Domain Expires Description be_typo_user TYPO3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is set by our CMS provider; TYPO3 and is used to identify a backend session when a Backend User is logged in to TYPO3 Backend or Frontend. fe_typo_user Typo3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is associated with the Typo3 web content management system. It is generally used as a user session identifier to enable user preferences to be stored, but in many cases it may not actually be needed as it can be set by default by the platform, though this can be prevented by site administrators. In most cases it is set to be destroyed at the end of a browser session. It contains a random identifier rather than any specific user data. ASP.NET_SessionId Microsoft Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written with Miscrosoft .NET based technologies. Usually used to maintain an anonymised user session by the server. JSESSIONID Oracle Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written in JSP. Usually used to maintain an anonymous user session by the server. ARRAffinity Microsoft Corporation .mitstudie.au.dk Session This cookie is set by websites run on the Windows Azure cloud platform. It is used for load balancing to make sure the visitor page requests are routed to the same server in any browsing session. esctx Microsoft Corporation .login.microsoftonline.com Session This cookie is used by Microsoft to securely verify your login information fpc Microsoft Corporation login.microsoftonline.com 4 weeks 2 days This cookie is used by Microsoft to securely verify your login information __cf_bm Cloudflare Inc. .pure.au.dk 29 minutes 59 seconds This cookie is used to distinguish between humans and bots. This is beneficial for the website, in order to make valid reports on the use of their website. __Secure-typo3nonce_ouB7_tePaslDY7zpIHG6wg aias.au.dk Session __cf_bm Cloudflare Inc. .linkedin.com 29 minutes 59 seconds This cookie is used to distinguish between humans and bots. This is beneficial for the website, in order to make valid reports on the use of their website. __cf_bm Cloudflare Inc. .twitter.com 29 minutes 58 seconds This cookie is used to distinguish between humans and bots. This is beneficial for the website, in order to make valid reports on the use of their website. ARRAffinitySameSite Microsoft Corporation .ofn.au.dk Session When using Microsoft Azure as a hosting platform and enabling load balancing, this cookie ensures that  requests from one visitor browsing session are always handled by the same server in the cluster. cf_clearance Cloudflare, Inc. .podbean.com 1 year This cookie is used by the CloudFlare service to identify trusted web traffic and override any security restrictions based on the visitor's IP address. It is essential for supporting a website's security features and in providing protection against malicious visitors. ARRAffinitySameSite Microsoft Corporation .docs.workzone.kmd.net Session When using Microsoft Azure as a hosting platform and enabling load balancing, this cookie ensures that  requests from one visitor browsing session are always handled by the same server in the cluster. XSRF-TOKEN event.au.dk 1 hour 59 minutes This cookie is written to help with site security in preventing Cross-Site Request Forgery attacks. li_gc LinkedIn Corporation .linkedin.com 5 months 4 weeks Used to store guest consent to the use of cookies for non-essential purposes x-ms-gateway-slice Microsoft Corporation login.microsoftonline.com Session Identifies a gateway for load balancing. CFTOKEN Adobe Inc. eddiprod.au.dk Session Cookie set by Adobe ColdFusion applications. Used in conjunction with CFID this cookie helps to uniquely identify a client device (browser) to enable the site to maintain user session variables. How those are used are specific to the site. CFTOKEN contains a random number to identify the client. brwConsent .airtable.com 5 minutes This cookie is used to record the user's consent to the use of cookies on the website, ensuring compliance with the website's privacy policy by remembering the user's preferences and consent state regarding cookies. CFTOKEN Adobe Inc. mit.au.dk Session Cookie set by Adobe ColdFusion applications. Used in conjunction with CFID this cookie helps to uniquely identify a client device (browser) to enable the site to maintain user session variables. How those are used are specific to the site. CFTOKEN contains a random number to identify the client. OptanonAlertBoxClosed OneTrust LLC .pure.au.dk 1 year This cookie is set by websites using certain versions of the cookie law compliance solution from OneTrust. It is set after visitors have seen a cookie information notice and in some cases only when they actively close the notice down. It enables the website not to show the message more than once to a user. The cookie has a one year lifespan and contains no personal information. PHPSESSID PHP.net internationalstaff.app3.geckobooking.dk Session Cookie generated by applications based on the PHP language. This is a general purpose identifier used to maintain user session variables. It is normally a random generated number, how it is used can be specific to the site, but a good example is maintaining a logged-in status for a user between pages. ARRAffinity Microsoft Corporation .ofn.au.dk Session This cookie is set by websites run on the Windows Azure cloud platform. It is used for load balancing to make sure the visitor page requests are routed to the same server in any browsing session. JSESSIONID Oracle Corporation .www.linkedin.com Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written in JSP. Usually used to maintain an anonymous user session by the server. ASPSESSIONIDSQQCSQRC webforms.au.dk Session This cookie name is generally associated with use as a general purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written with Microsoft ASP based technologies. The structure of the cookie name is a common root - ASPSESSIONID, followed by a series of unique letters. It is usually used to maintain an anonymised user session by the server. __RequestVerificationToken Microsoft Corporation forms.cloud.microsoft Session This is an anti-forgery cookie set by web applications built using ASP.NET MVC technologies. It is designed to stop unauthorised posting of content to a website, known as Cross-Site Request Forgery. It holds no information about the user and is destroyed on closing the browser. ARRAffinitySameSite Microsoft Corporation .mitstudie.au.dk Session When using Microsoft Azure as a hosting platform and enabling l