    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/innovation-facilitators-at-faculty-of-science-aarhus-university": {
      "title": "Innovation Specialists",
      "description": "Innovation Specialists at Faculty of Natural Sciences, Aarhus University - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU Danish website You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability Campus development History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Science Bridge Innovation Specialists at Faculty of Natural Sciences, Aarhus University Deadline 15 Sep 23:59 CEST Expected start 1 Dec Science Bridge Ny Munkegade 116 8000 Aarhus C Full-time position ID: 165085 Apply Are you passionate about research and innovation? Would you like to help translate excellent natural science research into value for society and industry to an even greater extent? Then you have a unique opportunity to join Science Bridge as an Innovation specialist. Science Bridge is a new strategic initiative at the Faculty of Natural Sciences, Aarhus University, established to strengthen the connection between research and society by promoting early and systematic knowledge exchange. The aim is to enable more research results to contribute with innovative responses to key societal challenges. We are looking to recruit up to four Innovation specialists for Science Bridge. Expected start date and duration of employment These are permanent positions and the expected start date is 1 December 2026. Responsibilities and tasks As an Innovation specialist in Science Bridge, you will work at the forefront of innovation, collaboration and societal engagement. You will support researchers across the faculty’s scientific disciplines in building bridges between research, industry, and society. You will play a key role in initiating, structuring, and maintaining interdisciplinary and cross-sector collaborations. In close interaction with researchers and external partners, you will identify collaboration opportunities, act as a “translator” between academic and non-academic contexts and ensure progress and continuity within and across defined focus areas known as Actions. Your main tasks will include: Initiating relationships with relevant internal and external partners and contributing to the development and maintenance of strong collaborations in close cooperation with the faculty’s research environments and existing professional networks Initiating, structuring and driving Actions – smaller, interdisciplinary collaborations where researchers and external partners share knowledge and jointly explore specific challenges Supporting the establishment of collaborations and consortia with the aim of preparing joint applications to private foundations, Innovation Fund Denmark and Horizon Europe Facilitating dialogue and matchmaking between researchers and relevant companies, organisations and public authorities Contributing to a culture where collaboration, knowledge exchange and entrepreneurship are an integrated part of research and education across the faculty Your profile We are looking for candidates with a strong interest in bridging science and the early stages of innovation and who are motivated by turning strategic ambitions into concrete activities and collaborations. Candidates should: Have experience with process management, innovation and strategic development Are motivated by creating results at the intersection between research and application Have experience working in or with research environments; experience with collaboration between research and industry (e.g. from a company, organisation or research institution) is an advantage Are able to identify and develop the potential of research ideas and connect them to societal and industry needs Are proactive, relationship-oriented and a strong communicator who can navigate across disciplines Preferably have experience with fundraising and proposal development in relation to national or European programmes, although this is not a requirement Work in a structured, proactive and results-oriented manner Have a high level of proficiency in English; Non-Danish speaking candidates must be willing to learn Danish within two years. Danish language training will be provided. What we offer You will join a newly established team of Innovation specialists at Science Bridge. The ideal team will represent diverse competences, including natural sciences but not limited to this, and ideally multiple nationalities. In addition, we aim to build a team with strong, collective knowledge of both the Danish research and innovation landscape– including funding schemes and industry – as well as European companies and funding opportunities. As an Innovation specialist, you will be part of the Science Bridge secretariat, which will also include a Director, a Head of Secretariat and a small number of additional staff. As Science Bridge is a newly established unit, you will have a real opportunity to shape the team’s tasks, structure and focus. There will also be good opportunities for professional development. Application If you believe you have the qualifications we are looking for and would like to make a difference at the interface between research and society, we encourage you to apply. The recruitment process includes two rounds of interviews. Candidates selected for the second round will complete a personality assessment. Interviews are expected to take place in late September or early October 2026. Place of work and area of employment The place of work is at Gustav Wieds Vej 14, 8000 Aarhus C, and the area of employment is Aarhus University with affiliated institutions. Contact information For further information, please contact Acting Director of Science Bridge, Vice-Dean Ole Bækgaard Nielsen, obn@au.dk; +45 60202674 or Head of Secretariat Annette Wandahl, awa@inano.au.dk; +45 23382280 Deadline Applications must be received no later than 15 September 2026. Formalities and salary range Salary and terms as agreed between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Confederation of Professional Unions. You will be employed as a Special consultant or Senior consultant. The base salary as a Special consultant is 450.909,00 and the base salary for a Senior consultant is 485.345,00. Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Ole Bækgaard Nielsen Vice-Dean, career development and innovation, Dean's Office, Natural Sciences +4560202674 obn@au.dk Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Nat-Tech Administrative Centre - Nat-Tech HR +4530783166 nat-tech.HR.team1@au.dk Apply Deadline: \n                            Tuesday 15 Sep 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: au@au.dk Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48 English Danish Cookies improve user experience When you click 'Accept all' cookies, Aarhus University can give you the best user experience. Cookies store information about how a user interacts with a website. All your data is anonymised and cannot be used to identify you. You can always change your consent again under ‘Cookies' in the website footer. The university uses its own cookies and cookies set by our partners. Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified Save & Close Accept all Decline all Read more about cookies Hide details List of cookies Cookie Policy Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified These cookies make it possible to use basic website functionality, e.g. navigation etc. The website does not work without these cookies. Cookie report Name Provider / Domain Expires Description be_typo_user TYPO3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is set by our CMS provider; TYPO3 and is used to identify a backend session when a Backend User is logged in to TYPO3 Backend or Frontend. fe_typo_user Typo3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is associated with the Typo3 web content management system. It is generally used as a user session identifier to enable user preferences to be stored, but in many cases it may not actually be needed as it can be set by default by the platform, though this can be prevented by site administrators. In most cases it is set to be destroyed at the end of a browser session. It contains a random identifier rather than any specific user data. ASP.NET_SessionId Microsoft Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written with Miscrosoft .NET based technologies. Usually used to maintain an anonymised user session by the server. JSESSIONID Oracle Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written in JSP. Usually used to maintain an anonymous user session by the server. ARRAffinity Microsoft Corporation .mitstudie.au.dk Session This cookie is set by websites run on the Windows Azure cloud platform. It is used for load balancing to make sure the visitor page requests are routed to the same server in any browsing session. esctx Microsoft Corporation .login.microsoftonline.com Session This cookie is used by Microsoft to securely verify your login information fpc Microsoft Corporation login.microsoftonline.com 4 weeks 2 days This cookie is used by Microsoft to securely verify your login information __cf_bm Cloudflare Inc. .pure.au.dk 29 minutes 59 seconds This cookie is used to distinguish between humans and bots. This is beneficial for the website, in order to make valid reports on the use of their website. __Secure-typo3nonce_ouB7_tePaslDY7zpIHG6wg aias.au.dk Session __cf_bm Cloudflare Inc. .linkedin.com 29 minutes 59 seconds This cookie is used to distinguish between humans and bots. This is beneficial for the website, in order to make valid reports on the use of their website. __cf_bm Cloudflare Inc. .twitter.com 29 minutes 58 seconds This cookie is used to distinguish between humans and bots. This is beneficial for the website, in order to make valid reports on the use of their website. ARRAffinitySameSite Microsoft Corporation .ofn.au.dk Session When using Microsoft Azure as a hosting platform and enabling load balancing, this cookie ensures that  requests from one visitor browsing session are always handled by the same server in the cluster. cf_clearance Cloudflare, Inc. .podbean.com 1 year This cookie is used by the CloudFlare service to identify trusted web traffic and override any security restrictions based on the visitor's IP address. It is essential for supporting a website's security features and in providing protection against malicious visitors. ARRAffinitySameSite Microsoft Corporation .docs.workzone.kmd.net Session When using Microsoft Azure as a hosting platform and enabling load balancing, this cookie ensures that  requests from one visitor browsing session are always handled by the same server in the cluster. XSRF-TOKEN event.au.dk 1 hour 59 minutes This cookie is written to help with site security in preventing Cross-Site Request Forgery attacks. li_gc LinkedIn Corporation .linkedin.com 5 months 4 weeks Used to store guest consent to the use of cookies for non-essential purposes x-ms-gateway-slice Microsoft Corporation login.microsoftonline.com Session Identifies a gateway for load balancing. CFTOKEN Adobe Inc. eddiprod.au.dk Session Cookie set by Adobe ColdFusion applications. Used in conjunction with CFID this cookie helps to uniquely identify a client device (browser) to enable the site to maintain user session variables. How those are used are specific to the site. CFTOKEN contains a random number to identify the client. brwConsent .airtable.com 5 minutes This cookie is used to record the user's consent to the use of cookies on the website, ensuring compliance with the website's privacy policy by remembering the user's preferences and consent state regarding cookies. CFTOKEN Adobe Inc. mit.au.dk Session Cookie set by Adobe ColdFusion applications. Used in conjunction with CFID this cookie helps to uniquely identify a client device (browser) to enable the site to maintain user session variables. How those are used are specific to the site. CFTOKEN contains a random number to identify the client. OptanonAlertBoxClosed OneTrust LLC .pure.au.dk 1 year This cookie is set by websites using certain versions of the cookie law compliance solution from OneTrust. It is set after visitors have seen a cookie information notice and in some cases only when they actively close the notice down. It enables the website not to show the message more than once to a user. The cookie has a one year lifespan and contains no personal information. PHPSESSID PHP.net internationalstaff