    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/postdoc-position-with-novo-nordisk-foundation-research-co2-center-aarhus-university-denmark": {
      "title": "Postdoc Position with Novo Nordisk Foundation Research CO2 Center Aarhus University, Denmark",
      "description": "Postdoc Position with Novo Nordisk Foundation Research CO2 Center Aarhus University, Denmark - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU Danish website You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability Campus development History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Chemistry - Department of Chemistry - CORC Postdoc Position with Novo Nordisk Foundation Research CO2 Center Aarhus University, Denmark Deadline 22 Sep 23:59 CEST Expected start 1 Dec Department of Chemistry - Department of Chemistry - CORC Gustav Wieds Vej 10C 8000 Aarhus C Fixed term full-time position 1 Dec 2026 - 30 Nov 2028 ID: 167617 Apply Postdoc Position with Novo Nordisk Foundation Research CO2 at Aarhus University, Denmark The Novo Nordisk Foundation is establishing a world-leading interdisciplinary research center to develop knowledge and technology to capture and recycle carbon dioxide. The center will be based at Aarhus University in Denmark and will collaborate with industry and authorities to identify new solutions to reduce atmospheric CO2 levels. The electrochemical section, led by Professor Kim Daasbjerg, is seeking candidates for a two-year postdoc position at this CO2 center. The postdoc position is available from December 01, 2026, or as soon as possible thereafter. Your tasks The successful candidate will conduct research on developing catalysts for bicarbonate conversion using electrochemical methods. The focus will be on designing the interfacial organic layer at the electrode surface to promote the selective reduction of CO2 to syngas or ethylene. In addition, the most promising processes will be scaled up using electrochemical flow cells. This work will be carried out in collaboration with other members of the Daasbjerg research group. Your requirements The successful candidate is required to have a strong background in electrochemistry must be familiar with catlysis for carrying out chemical transactions must have a PhD degree in Chemistry or similar is expected to have significant experience in flow technology must have experience with international collaborations and serve as a mentor/leader for the research group Who are we The Department of Chemistry is among the most successful departments in the Faculty of Natural Sciences at Aarhus University. The department houses several of the Danish National Research Foundation’s Centers of Excellence and teaches many of the faculty's degree programs. Comprising a wide range of scientific areas, the department is a strong partner in interdisciplinary initiatives, especially in the Novo Nordisk Foundation CO2 Research Center. The Department of Chemistry also educates most chemists in Denmark, with well over 200 active BSc students, a considerable number of MSc students, and more than 100 PhD students. The department has 42 permanent academic staff members, a strong support organization, and a considerable number of affiliated researchers. What we offer The successful candidate is offered: access to a well-developed research infrastructure laboratory space, shared equipment a research climate inviting lively, open, and critical discussion within and across different fields of research a working environment with teamwork, close working relations, network activities among young scientists, and social activities a workplace characterized by professionalism, equality, and a healthy work-life balance Place of work The place of work is Gustav Wieds Vej 10, 8000 Aarhus C, and the area of employment is Aarhus University with affiliated institutions. Contact information For further information, please contact Professor Kim Daasbjerg at +45 23485249 or kdaa@chem.au.dk. Application deadline Applications must be received no later than 22 September 2026. Application procedure Shortlisting is used. This means that after the deadline for applications – and with the assistance from the assessment committee chairman, and the appointment committee if necessary, – the head of department selects the candidates to be evaluated. All applicants will be notified whether or not their applications have been sent to an expert assessment committee for evaluation. The selected applicants will be informed about the composition of the committee, and each applicant is given the opportunity to comment on the part of the assessment that concerns him/her self. Formalities and salary range Natural Sciences refers to the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Danish Universities under the Danish Ministry of Science, Technology and Innovation . The application must be in English and include a curriculum vitae, degree certificate, a complete list of publications, a statement of future research plans and information about research activities, teaching portfolio and verified information on previous teaching experience (if any). Guidelines for applicants can be found here. Appointment shall be in accordance with the collective labour agreement between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations. Further information on qualification requirements and job content may be found in the Memorandum on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Danish Universities . Salary and terms as agreed between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Confederation of Professional Unions at basic salary steps 4-8. Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. Research activities will be evaluated in relation to actual research time. Thus, we encourage applicants to specify periods of leave without research activities, in order to be able to subtract these periods from the span of the scientific career during the evaluation of scientific productivity. Aarhus University offers a broad variety of services for international researchers and accompanying families, including relocation service and career counselling to expat partners. Read more here . Please find more information about entering and working in Denmark here . Aarhus University also offers a Junior Researcher Development Programme targeted at career development for postdocs at AU. You can read more about it here . At the Faculty of Natural Science at Aarhus University, we strive to support our scientific staff in their career development. We focus on competency development and career clarification and want to make your opportunities transparent. On our website , you can find information on all types of scientific positions, as well as the entry criteria we use when assessing candidates. You can also read more about how we can assist you in your career planning and development. The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Kim Daasbjerg Professor, Department of Chemistry - Department of Chemistry - CORC +4523485249 kdaa@chem.au.dk Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Nat-Tech Administrative Centre - Nat-Tech HR +4520735558 nat-tech.HR.team1@au.dk Apply Deadline: \n                            Tuesday 22 Sep 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: au@au.dk Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48 English Danish Cookies improve user experience When you click 'Accept all' cookies, Aarhus University can give you the best user experience. Cookies store information about how a user interacts with a website. All your data is anonymised and cannot be used to identify you. You can always change your consent again under ‘Cookies' in the website footer. The university uses its own cookies and cookies set by our partners. Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified Save & Close Accept all Decline all Read more about cookies Hide details List of cookies Cookie Policy Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified These cookies make it possible to use basic website functionality, e.g. navigation etc. The website does not work without these cookies. Cookie report Name Provider / Domain Expires Description be_typo_user TYPO3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is set by our CMS provider; TYPO3 and is used to identify a backend session when a Backend User is logged in to TYPO3 Backend or Frontend. fe_typo_user Typo3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is associated with the Typo3 web content management system. It is generally used as a user session identifier to enable user preferences to be stored, but in many cases it may not actually be needed as it can be set by default by the platform, though this can be prevented by site administrators. In most cases it is set to be destroyed at the end of a browser session. It contains a random identifier rather than any specific user data. ASP.NET_SessionId Microsoft Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written with Miscrosoft .NET based technologies. Usually used to maintain an anonymised user session by the server. JSESSIONID Oracle Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written in JSP. Usually used to maintain an anonymous user session by the server. ARRAffinity Microsoft Corporation .mitstudie.au.dk Session This cookie is set by websites run on the Windows Azure cloud platform. It is used for load balancing to make sure the visitor page requests are routed to the same server in any browsing session. esctx Microsoft Corporation .login.microsoftonline.com Session This cookie is used by Microsoft to securely verify your login information fpc Microsoft Corporation login.microsoftonline.com 4 weeks 2 days This cookie is used by Microsoft to securely verify your login information __cf_bm Cloudflare Inc. .pure.au.dk 29 minutes 59 seconds This cookie is used to distinguish between humans and bots. This is beneficial for the website, in order to make valid reports on the use of their website. __Secure-typo3nonce_ouB7_tePaslDY7zpIHG6wg aias.au.dk Session __cf_bm Cloudflare Inc. .linkedin.com 29 minutes 59 seconds This cookie is used to distinguish between humans and bots. This is beneficial for the website, in order to make valid reports on the use of their website. __cf_bm Cloudflare Inc. .twitter.com 29 minutes 58 seconds This cookie is used to distinguish between humans and bots. This is beneficial for the website, in order to make valid reports on the use of their website. ARRAffinitySameSite Microsoft Corporation .ofn.au.dk Session When using Microsoft Azure as a hosting platform and enabling load balancing, this cookie ensures that  requests from one visitor browsing session are always handled by the same server in the cluster. cf_clearance Cloudflare, Inc. .podbean.com 1 year This cookie is used by the CloudFlare service to identify trusted web traffic and override any security restrictions based on the visitor's IP address. It is essential for supporting a website's security features and in providing protection against malicious visitors. ARRAffinitySameSite Microsoft Corporation .docs.workzone.kmd.net Session When using Microsoft Azure as a hosting platform and enabling load balancing, this cookie ensures that  requests from one visitor browsing session are always handled by the same server in the cluster. XSRF-TOKEN event.au.dk 1 hour 59 minutes This cookie is written to help with site security in preventing Cross-Site Request Forgery attacks. li_gc LinkedIn Corporation .linkedin.com 5 months 4 weeks Used to store guest consent to the use of cookies for non-essential purposes x-ms-gateway-slice Microsoft Corporation login.microsoftonline.com Session Identifies a gateway for load balancing. CFTOKEN Adobe Inc. eddiprod.au.dk Session Cookie set by Adobe ColdFusion applications. Used in conjunction with CFID this cookie helps to uniquely identify a client device (browser) to enable the site to maintain user session variables. How those are used are specific to the site. CFTOKEN contains a random number to identify the client. brwConsent .airtable.com 5 minutes This cookie is used to record the user's consent to the use of cookies on the website, ensuring compliance with the website's privacy policy by remembering the user's preferences and consent state regarding cookies. CFTOKEN Adobe Inc. mit.au.dk Session Cookie set by Adobe ColdFusion applications. Used in conjunction with CFID this cookie helps to uniquely identify a client device (browser) to enable the site to maintain user session variables. How those are used are specific to the site. CFTOKEN contains a random number to identify the client. OptanonAlertBoxClosed OneTrust LLC .pure.au.dk 1 year This cookie is set by websites using certain versions of the cookie law compliance solution from OneTrust. It is set after visitors have seen a cookie information notice and in some cases only when they actively close the notice down. It enables the website not to show the message more than once to a user. The cookie has a one year lifespan and contains no personal information. PHPSESSID PHP.net internationalstaff.app3.geckobooking.dk Session Cookie generated by applications based on the PHP language. This is a general purpose identifier used to maintain user session variables. It is normally a random generated number, how it is used can be specific to the site, but a good example is maintaining a logged-in status for a user between pages. ARRAffinity Microsoft Corporation .ofn.au.dk Session This cookie is set by websites run on the Windows Azure cloud platform. It is used for load balancing to make sure the visitor page requests are routed to the same server in any browsing session. JSESSIONID Oracle Corporation .www.linkedin.com Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written in JSP. Usually used to maintain an anonymous user session by the server. ASPSESSIONIDSQQCSQRC webforms.au.dk Session This cookie name is generally associated with use as a general purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written with Microsoft ASP based technologies. The structure of the cookie name is a common root - ASPSESSIONID, followed by a series of unique letters. It is usually used to maintain an anonymised user session by the server. __RequestVerificationToken Microsoft Corporation forms.cloud.microsoft Session This is an anti-forgery cookie set by web applications built using ASP.NET MVC technologies. It is designed to stop unauthorised posting of content to a website, known as Cross-Site Request Forgery. It holds no information about the user and is destroyed on closing the browser. ARRAffinitySameSit