rveyIT-HAProxy-surveyxact_frontend survey.au.dk Session esctx-nfHdeloMxho .login.microsoftonline.com Session __Secure-ROLLOUT_TOKEN .youtube.com 5 months 4 weeks msal.cache.encryption forms.cloud.microsoft Session Queue-it-audk________________audkprod2026 audk.queue-it.net 1 day productCode soeg.kb.dk Session __Secure-UqZBpD3n3naPU20-9Fvn5i-TSO9FpchbYtbA9YCEpg3UXgo_ soeg.kb.dk 1 year esctx-O2uzNWDgQPY .login.microsoftonline.com Session esctx-cnOtbYn1wEE .login.microsoftonline.com Session What is a cookie? A cookie is a text file, that is stored on your computer, mobile or similar device. When visiting our website it is sent forth and back between your browser and a web server. It is used by AU or a third party, which is described more specific under the cookie descriptions at the bottom of this page. Cookies cannot contain malicious code such as virus. Cookies can be either temporary or permanent. The temporary cookies are linked to one specific visit, and are deleted again when you close the website. The permanent cookie is saved on your computer, mobile or tablet for a period of time. How long the various cookies remain is described in the cookie descriptions at the bottom of the page. Each time you visit the website, however, the cookie will be renewed and the period will thus start all over again. What data is collected via cookies? Most cookies collect anonymous data, such as the amount of time of your visit to the website, what pages you have visited, whether your computer, tablet or smartphone has used the pages before, which website you came from, which browser and operating system you use and the like. In some cases, IP addresses are also collected, which are personally identifiable data. Therefore, you can also read our Privacy Policy , which tells how we at AU process personal information. If any of the third party services, we use, process data on behalf of AU, we will, if possible, enter into a Data Processing Agreement with them. The supplier is thus not allowed to use the data for their own purposes or to pass them on to others. Delete cookies It is also possible to delete or block cookies. See the guide: https://www.allaboutcookies.org/manage-cookies/clear-cookies-installed.html The website is owned and published by: Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 DK-8000 Aarhus C Tel. no: 87 15 00 00 Email: au@au.dk Cookies consent ID : Cookie report created by CookieScript"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/research/researcher-positions/howtoapply": {
      "title": "How to apply for an academic position",
      "description": "How to apply for an academic position Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU Danish website You are here: AU Research Researcher positions How to apply Research Research units and facilities PhD programmes Researcher positions Attractive working conditions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher Development Programme How to apply for an academic position Photo: AU Photo You find available positions under Vacant positions on our website. Each job advertisement contains all necessary information on how to apply. The application The application and all relevant documents must be submitted via AU’s online recruitment system.  When you have submitted your application, you will receive an email verification in your inbox notifying you that the university has received the application. If you encounter any technical difficulties, please contact the relevant HR-department mentioned in the job advertisement. The application must include the documents and attachments specified in the job advertisement, typically: Application including motivation for applying for the position and your contribution to and visions for the position. CV Diploma Documentation for your academic qualifications List of publications Publications including co-authorship declaration Teaching portfolio The next steps in the process After the application deadline, an appointment committee advises the head of department on which applicants are the best overall match for the position. Through this shortlisting process, the head of department selects the applicants who will receive a thorough assessment of their professional qualifications. The assessment committee will then assess these applicants. The shortlisting process may differ from faculty to faculty. If your application is not shortlisted for assessment , HR will inform you immediately after the shortlisting process is completed. Final rejections are sent at the end of the recruitment process. If you are shortlisted for assessment , you will receive an answer by HR containing information about the assessment committee. The next step is the job interview. Prior to the interviews, you  may be called in to an event at the department, for example a lecture, a meeting with permanent academic staff, etc. so that you and the department management may  gain an impression of each other and you get an idea of  the tasks involved in the position. Finally, the head of department will contact you to tell you whether you are accepted for the position or not. The employment process differs from faculty to faculty and depending on the type of position. The final candidate who is offered the position will be contacted regarding: Certificate of employment Work and residence permit Holiday scheme Pension scheme Tax scheme The recruitment process for academic positions at AU takes three to six months, depending on the type of position. Guidelines and specific application requirements for academic positions The Faculty of Arts Aarhus School of Business and Social Sciences The Faculty of Health The Faculty of Natural Sciences The Facultry of Technical Sciences Revised\n    26.06.2026 - International Staff Office Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: au@au.dk Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 118190 / i48 English Danish Cookies improve user experience When you click 'Accept all' cookies, Aarhus University can give you the best user experience. Cookies store information about how a user interacts with a website. All your data is anonymised and cannot be used to identify you. You can always change your consent again under ‘Cookies' in the website footer. The university uses its own cookies and cookies set by our partners. Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified Save & Close Accept all Decline all Read more about cookies Hide details List of cookies Cookie Policy Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified These cookies make it possible to use basic website functionality, e.g. navigation etc. The website does not work without these cookies. Cookie report Name Provider / Domain Expires Description be_typo_user TYPO3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is set by our CMS provider; TYPO3 and is used to identify a backend session when a Backend User is logged in to TYPO3 Backend or Frontend. fe_typo_user Typo3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is associated with the Typo3 web content management system. It is generally used as a user session identifier to enable user preferences to be stored, but in many cases it may not actually be needed as it can be set by default by the platform, though this can be prevented by site administrators. In most cases it is set to be destroyed at the end of a browser session. It contains a random identifier rather than any specific user data. ASP.NET_SessionId Microsoft Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written with Miscrosoft .NET based technologies. Usually used to maintain an anonymised user session by the server. JSESSIONID Oracle Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written in JSP. Usually used to maintain an anonymous user session by the server. ARRAffinity Microsoft Corporation .mitstudie.au.dk Session This cookie is set by websites run on the Windows Azure cloud platform. It is used for load balancing to make sure the visitor page requests are routed to the same server in any browsing sess