    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/associate-professor-in-translational-optical-blood-flow-imaging-and-microvascular-dynamics": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in translational optical blood flow imaging and microvascular dynamics",
      "description": "Associate Professor in translational optical blood flow imaging and microvascular dynamics - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Clinical Medicine - Center of Functionally Integrative Neuroscience, AUH - Faculty: Health Sciences Associate Professor in translational optical blood flow imaging and microvascular dynamics Deadline 23 Sep 23:59 CEST Expected start 1 Feb Department of Clinical Medicine - Center of Functionally Integrative Neuroscience, AUH Palle Juul-Jensens Boulevard 99 8200 Aarhus N Fixed term full-time position 1 Feb 2027 - 31 Jul 2028 ID: 168724 Apply The Centre of Functionally Integrative Neuroscience (CFIN) at the Department of Clinical Medicine, Faculty of Health Sciences, Aarhus University invites applications for a position as Associate Professor in the field of microvascular dynamics research and translational non-invasive optical blood flow imaging as per 1 February 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. The position is an 18 months fixed-term full-time position. As an Associate Professor at the Department of Clinical Medicine, you will be part of what is probably the largest health science research department in Denmark. Our clinical research covers all the medical specialities and takes place in close collaboration with the university hospital and the regional hospitals in the Central Denmark Region. We have approx. 30,000 square metres of modern research facilities for experimental surgery and medicine, animal facilities and also advanced scanners at our disposal. The department has overall responsibility for the Master's degree programs in medicine and in molecular medicine. At the department we are approx. 670 academic employees, 500 PhD students and 160 technical/administrative employees who are cooperating across disciplines. As an Associate Professor, you will be working at Aarhus University Hospital or another hospital in the Central Denmark Region. You can read more about the department here and about the faculty here . Your job responsibilities As Associate Professor in microvascular research and non-invasive optical blood flow imaging , you will contribute to the department’s research and teaching environment and to the faculty’s overall research strategy. You will contribute to the development of the department both individually and in collaboration with others via your research of high international quality. You ensure that your teaching maintains a high academic and didactic standard. You possess professional collaborative skills and a broad academic network which you are able to bring into play in your contribution to the academic development of Aarhus University and its profile both nationally and internationally. Your main tasks will consist of: Developing Dynamic Light Scattering techniques for imaging of brain and systemic perfusion and oxygenation, including Laser Speckle Contrast Imaging, Dynamic Light Scattering Imaging and Hyperspectral Imaging. Leading research projects aimed to characterize microvascular abnormalities in dementia and associated risk factors in relevant animal models and in patients. Establishing translational approaches for neurovascular research with non-invasive optical imaging. Research of high international quality, including publication in top international journals and communicating your research in national and international academic networks. Teaching and supervision of Bachelor’s and Master's degree students and contribution to the development of new teaching activities. To contribute to the funding with the help of external research funding. Supervision of PhD students and contributing to the development of the faculty's PhD courses. Involvement in assessment and committee work at Aarhus University. Dissemination of your research to the outside world. You will report to professor Leif Østergaard. Your competences You have established yourself as a prominent researcher within non-invasive optical blood flow imaging and microvascular research, and you possess documented solid research and teaching qualifications at a high international level. You have broad international cooperative partnerships and experience of research partnerships with private and public-sector stakeholders, and you have as experience as a skilled group leader. At the same time, you have experience of attracting significant research funding from national and international funding bodies. We draw attention to a stay or employment at least one internationally recognised research institution. You have documented world-leading expertise in developing and applying dynamic light scattering imaging techniques: a deep understanding of light scattering and speckle theory, engineering and data science skills, and vast experience in applying those techniques to study microvasculature (brain perfusion in particular). As a person, you are dedicated and a skilled communicator. You are able to build relationships based on trust with students, colleagues and partners. As a lecturer, you communicate the newest and relevant knowledge in a committed, clear and comprehensible manner. As a supervisor, you are professional, inspiring and inclusive. You are ready to take co-responsibility for the development of the department's research and education at the highest international level and for ensuring that we maintain a good work environment. You naturally involve yourself in interdisciplinary collaboration at departmental, faculty and university level as well as nationally and internationally. We expect you to be fluent in oral and written English. International applicants are expected to learn Danish, and Aarhus University arranges Danish teaching. In order to be assessed as qualified for an Associate Professor position, you must meet these academic criteria . Questions about the position If you have any questions about the position, please contact Leif Østergaard at phone: +45 7846 4091. Your place of work will be CFIN, Department of Clinical Medicine, Aarhus University and Aarhus University Hospital, Universitetsbyen 3, Building 1710 8000 Aarhus C. Terms of employment Appointment as an associate professor requires research and teaching qualifications at the level that can be achieved through the satisfactory completion of a period of appointment as an assistant professor, but may also be obtained in other ways. The applicant is required to have completed a university pedagogical programme or an equivalent programme. Further information on the appointment procedure can be found in the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities . The appointment is in accordance with the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations (Akademikerne). Remuneration is in accordance with the above, and the Salary agreement catalogue for staff at Health . The yearly base salary for a fulltime associate professor is DKK 706.233,06 (including a position related supplement, a pre-agreed associate professor supplememt and pension (18.07%)). Additional supplement(s) can be negotiated dependent on experience, special qualifications and performance of special functions. Authorisation supplement(s) will be granted, if relevant for the position. Your local eligible trade union representative at Aarhus University negotiates your salary on your behalf. Researchers recruited from abroad are offered a special researcher tax scheme with a lower tax rate. Travel and moving expenses may be covered according to the employee in question and, to a limited extent, the accompanying family. Further information on qualification requirements and job description can be found in the Ministerial order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities . Application Your application must include the following: Motivated application Curriculum Vitae Diploma Template for applicant - associate professor A list of publications A teaching portfolio. We refer to Guideline on the use of teaching portfolios The five publications stated as the most important in the 'Template for applicant - associate professor' must be submitted Research plan, which is part of the 'Template to applicant - associate professor' can be uploaded separately (optional) Coauthor statement(s) can be uploaded (optional) References/recommendations can be uploaded separately in the e-recruitment system (optional) We refer to the faculty’s Guidelines for applicants . Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. International applicant? Aarhus University offers a broad variety of services for international researchers and accompanying families, including assistance with relocation and career counselling to expat partners. Please find more information about the International Staff Office and the range of services here . The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Leif Østergaard Clinical Professor, Department of Clinical Medicine - Center of Functionally Integrative Neuroscience +4578464091 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Health Administrative Centre - Health HR +4593521835 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Wednesday 23 Sep 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/position-as-postdoc-in-biochemical-and-functional-characterization-of-milk-derived-extracellular-vesicles": {
      "title": "Questions about the position ?",
      "description": "Position as postdoc in Biochemical and functional characterization of milk-derived extracellular vesicles - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Molecular Health Position as postdoc in Biochemical and functional characterization of milk-derived extracellular vesicles Deadline 25 Sep 23:59 CEST Expected start 1 Dec Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Molecular Health Universitetsbyen 81 8000 Aarhus C Fixed term full-time position 1 Dec 2026 - 30 Nov 2028 ID: 167931 Apply Position as postdoc in Biochemical and functional characterization of milk-derived extracellular vesicles We are seeking applicants for a postdoc position in ‘’Biochemical and functional characterization of milk-derived extracellular vesicles” to join us at the Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics in the research team of Jan Trige Rasmussen. Expected start date and duration of employment The position is available from 1 December 2026 or as soon as possible hereafter. Duration of employment is two years. Job description We invite applications for a postdoctoral position in the interdisciplinary NNF-synergy project MEVIN (Milk Extracellular Vesicles for Preterm Infants). You will contribute to the biochemical and functional characterization of milk-derived extracellular vesicles (EVs) as a novel supplement for preterm infant nutrition. More specifically you will be involved identification and validation the most promising milk EV fractions for intestinal protection and immune regulation. We are looking for a postdoctoral researcher to join the interdisciplinary MEVIN project. You will contribute to the isolation, characterization, and functional analysis of milk EVs, especially from bovine sources, and investigate their RNA cargo, cellular uptake, and intracellular trafficking in recipient cells. The work spans biochemical and molecular characterisation using single-vesicle tracking, nanoparticle tracking analysis (NTA), NanoFlow cytometry, and advanced imaging techniques, as well as bioinformatic analysis of small RNAs and transcriptomic data. You will collaborate closely with partners working on animal models (preterm pigs) and clinical studies, contributing to the translation of milk EV biology into nutritional interventions for preterm infants, as well as preparation of data for high-quality publications and project reports. Your profile We are looking for a highly motivated candidate with a strong publication record and the following qualifications: PhD degree in molecular biology, biochemistry, nanoscience, biotechnology, immunology, or a closely related field. Documented hands-on experience with isolation and characterization of extracellular vesicles (e.g., size-exclusion chromatography, density-gradient centrifugation, NTA, immunoblotting, or nanoflow cytometry). Practical expertise in advanced imaging or single-particle analysis (e.g., cryo-EM/TEM, TIRF microscopy, single-vesicle tracking, confocal microscopy, or high-sensitivity flow cytometry). Solid skills in molecular biology and biochemistry and quantitative biomolecular analysis. Experience or knowledge related to RNA biology, EV surface engineering (e.g., fusion proteins or ligand display), affinity-based targeting, or cell-uptake assays will be an advantage. Excellent English communication skills, ability to work independently and responsibly, and a collaborative mindset in an international research environment. Self-driven and capable of independent research planning, while thriving in an international, collaborative, and interdisciplinary team environment. Who we are The postdoc will be affiliated to the Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics. The Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics is part of the Faculty of Natural Sciences, Aarhus University and comprises research within the areas of Plant Molecular Biology, Neurobiology, RNA Biology and Innovation, Protein Science, Cellular Health, Intervention and Nutrition. There are currently 75 full time scientific staff and 95 PhD students. The department is responsible for two educations: Molecular Biology and Molecular Medicine with a yearly uptake of 160 students in total. Please refer to http://mbg.au.dk/ for further information about The Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics and to https://nat.au.dk/ and http://www.au.dk/ for information on Faculty of Natural Sciences and Aarhus University, respectively. Place of work and area of employment The place of work is at departmental locations, Universitetsbyen 81/ Gustav Wieds Vej 14, 8000 Aarhus C, Denmark, and the area of employment is Aarhus University with related departments. Contact information For further information please contact Senior researcher Jan Trige Rasmussen., +45 87 16 89 98, [email protected] Deadline Applications must be received no later than 25 September 2026. Application procedure Shortlisting is used. This means that after the deadline for applications – and with the assistance from the assessment committee chairman, and the appointment committee if necessary, – the head of department selects the candidates to be evaluated. All applicants will be notified whether or not their applications have been sent to an expert assessment committee for evaluation. The selected applicants will be informed about the composition of the committee, and each applicant is given the opportunity to comment on the part of the assessment that concerns him/her self. Formalities and salary range Natural Sciences refers to the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Danish Universities under the Danish Ministry of Science, Technology and Innovation . The application must be in English and include a curriculum vitae, degree certificate, a complete list of publications, a statement of future research plans and information about research activities, teaching portfolio and verified information on previous teaching experience (if any). Guidelines for applicants can be found here. Appointment shall be in accordance with the collective labour agreement between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations. Further information on qualification requirements and job content may be found in the Memorandum on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Danish Universities . Salary and terms as agreed between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Confederation of Professional Unions at basic salary steps 4-8. Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. Research activities will be evaluated in relation to actual research time. Thus, we encourage applicants to specify periods of leave without research activities, in order to be able to subtract these periods from the span of the scientific career during the evaluation of scientific productivity. Aarhus University offers a broad variety of services for international researchers and accompanying families, including relocation service and career counselling to expat partners. Read more here . Please find more information about entering and working in Denmark here . Aarhus University also offers a Junior Researcher Development Programme targeted at career development for postdocs at AU. You can read more about it here . At the Faculty of Natural Science at Aarhus University, we strive to support our scientific staff in their career development. We focus on competency development and career clarification and want to make your opportunities transparent. On our website , you can find information on all types of scientific positions, as well as the entry criteria we use when assessing candidates. You can also read more about how we can assist you in your career planning and development. The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Jan Trige Rasmussen Senior Researcher, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Molecular Health +4528835104 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Nat-Tech Administrative Centre - Nat-Tech HR +4520735558 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Friday 25 Sep 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/student-assistant-in-administration-and-laboratory-work": {
      "title": "Student Assistant in Administration and Laboratory Work",
      "description": "Student Assistant in Administration and Laboratory Work - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Protein Science Student Assistant in Administration and Laboratory Work Deadline 25 Sep 23:59 CEST Expected start 15 Oct Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Protein Science Universitetsbyen 81 8000 Aarhus C Fixed term part-time position 15 Oct 2026 - 29 Jun 2027 5 hours per week ID: 168680 Apply The Plant-PATH Center of Excellence at the Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics (MBG), Aarhus University, is looking for a student assistant to support the Centre’s research activities. The position combines predominantly administrative support with some practical work in the laboratory. Tasks may include assisting with the day-to-day coordination and organisation of activities at the Centre, including supporting the center coordinator with administrative tasks, as well as some laboratory tasks related to the Centre’s research as needed. The position is a fixed-term, hourly paid student assistant position of approximately 5 hours per week. Expected start date and duration of employment This is a 8,5 month position from 15 October 2026, or as soon as possible thereafter. The position is a fixed-term position to end on 30 June 2027. Tasks As a Student Assistant at the Plant-PATH Center of Excellence, you will have the opportunity to contribute to both the administrative activities and the research environment of an international centre at Aarhus University. The position offers a varied combination of office-based tasks and hands-on laboratory work, providing insight into how a research centre operates and how scientific research is carried out. Your primary tasks will include: Providing administrative support for the day-to-day activities of the Plant-PATH Center Assisting with practical organisation and coordination of Centre activities Supporting researchers with routine laboratory tasks and other practical work Contributing to a well-organised and supportive working environment for the Centre's researchers All tasks will be carried out in close collaboration with members of the Plant-PATH research groups and the Centre Coordinator. Qualifications We are looking for a motivated and reliable student who is interested in gaining experience in both research support and the day-to-day activities of an international research centre. We expect that you: Are enrolled as a student, preferably within the natural sciences or a related field Have an interest in laboratory work and are comfortable working in a laboratory environment Are organised, responsible and able to work independently on assigned tasks Have a structured and flexible approach to both administrative and practical tasks Experience with research communication and website maintenance (Typo3) is an advantage Are able to collaborate effectively with researchers and colleagues from different backgrounds Have good written and oral communication skills in both Danish and English Who we are Plant-PATH – Center for Active Transport of Plant Hormones – is a Danish National Research Foundation Center of Excellence based at Aarhus University. We unite leading groups in Denmark, Belgium, and Germany in an international and collaborative research environment, offering excellent opportunities for training, exchange, and scientific development. We are hosted by the Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics, within the central campus of Aarhus University, comprising a vibrant research and education environment. The department currently has 75 full time scientific staff, 95 PhD students and a yearly uptake of around 160 students housed in the same building ensuring a lively setting. Plant-PATH Center website Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics website Place of work and area of employment The place of work is at Universitetsbyen 81, 8000 Aarhus C, and the area of employment is Aarhus University with affiliated institutions. Contact information For further information, please contact: Plant-PATH Center Coordinator, Leila Margot Henkes, +45 20 96 90 07, [email protected] . Deadline Applications must be received no later than 25 September 2026. Formalities and salary range Salary and terms as agreed between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Union of Commercial and Clerical Employees in Denmark/State (HK/Stat) for clerical staff, laboratory technicians and IT employees and the joint collective agreement concluded between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Organisations of Public Employees - Denmark - Danish State Sector (the OAO-S joint collective agreement). You must be enrolled as a student and provide documentation of enrollment at a higher education institution. Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Bjørn Panyella Pedersen Professor, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Protein Science +4529723499 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Nat-Tech Administrative Centre - Nat-Tech HR +4522228426 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Friday 25 Sep 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/part-time-it-developer-for-research-projects-at-department-of-electrical-and-computer-engineering": {
      "title": "Questions about the position ?",
      "description": "Part-Time IT-developer for Research Projects at Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering - Software Engineering & Computing systems Part-Time IT-developer for Research Projects at Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering Deadline 25 Sep 23:59 CEST Expected start 15 Nov Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering - Software Engineering & Computing systems Helsingforsgade 10 8200 Aarhus N Fixed term part-time position 15 Nov 2026 - 29 Jun 2027 10 hours per week ID: 168847 Apply Are you passionate about developing software for research projects? If so, the Software Engineering and Computing Systems section at the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering at Aarhus University is seeking a part-time IT-developer. This is a temporary position, starting on 15 November 2026, or as otherwise agreed, until 30 June 2027. Tasks You will be expected to contribute to, establish, and develop software and systems for use in various externally funded research projects. You will primarily work on software components used to develop proofs of concept for one or more research projects. You will be involved in various activities carried out as part of the relevant research projects, which may also include contributing to research papers. These activities will be carried out in close collaboration with the researchers working on the relevant projects. Your Profile Please indicate in your application whether you are currently studying and, if so, what you are studying. Have strong professional software-development skills (and possibly electronics skills as well). Work well with a team of colleagues from different disciplinary backgrounds. Are able to communicate effectively in both written and spoken English. Have a positive and approachable personality. The department/centre offers: Well-developed research infrastructure, laboratory facilities, and shared equipment. An exciting interdisciplinary environment with numerous national, international, and industry partners. A workplace culture that encourages lively, open, and critical discussion. A working environment with close professional relationships, networking opportunities, and social activities. A workplace characterised by professionalism, equality, and a healthy work–life balance. Workingplace The place of work is the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, Aarhus University, Finlandsgade 22, 8200 Aarhus N, Denmark. The scope of employment covers Aarhus University and its affiliated institutions. Contact information Further information can be obtained by contacting: Prasad Talasila [email protected] Deadline All applications must be received no later than 25 September 2026. Formalities and salary range The employment is subject to section 15 of the collective agreement for IT employees (PROSA) in the service of the state and LC/CO10-S (the Confederation of Teachers’ Unions/the Danish Confederation of Public Employees of 2010) collective agreement. Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Prasad Talasila Member of Administrative Staff, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering - Software Engineering & Computing systems - Edison [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Nat-Tech Administrative Centre - Nat-Tech HR +4522140468 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Friday 25 Sep 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
