    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/postdoc-positions-on-program-analysis-for-software-supply-chain-security-at-computer-science-aarhus-university": {
      "title": "Postdoc positions on Program Analysis for Software Supply Chain Security",
      "description": "Postdoc positions on Program Analysis for Software Supply Chain Security at Computer Science, Aarhus University - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Computer Science Postdoc positions on Program Analysis for Software Supply Chain Security at Computer Science, Aarhus University Deadline 13 Oct 23:59 CEST Expected start 1 Jan Department of Computer Science Åbogade 34 8200 Aarhus N Fixed term full-time position 1 Jan 2027 - 31 Dec 2028 ID: 169299 Apply The Department of Computer Science, Aarhus University invites applications for postdocs, funded by Professor Anders Møller’s ERC Advanced Grant project “Program Analysis for Software Supply Chain Security”. The postdocs will conduct research on program analysis within the Programming Languages, Logic, and Software Security research group at Aarhus University. The focus of the positions will be in developing new techniques for analyzing security of open-source components and large-scale applications. Applicants are expected to have a strong background in Programming Languages and Software Engineering, including experience with static program analysis. A PhD in Computer Science or a closely related field is required by the time of employment. Expected start date We offer full-time (37 hours/week) two-year postdoc positions. The starting date is January 1 2027 or later in 2027. Place of work The place of work is Department of Computer Science, Åbogade 34, 8200 Aarhus N. Contact information For more information, contact Professor Anders Møller at email: [email protected] or by phone: +4523309994. Application deadline Applications must be received no later than 13 October 2026. Application procedure Shortlisting is used. This means that after the deadline for applications – and with the assistance from the assessment committee chairman, and the appointment committee if necessary, – the head of department selects the candidates to be evaluated. All applicants will be notified whether or not their applications have been sent to an expert assessment committee for evaluation. The selected applicants will be informed about the composition of the committee, and each applicant is given the opportunity to comment on the part of the assessment that concerns him/her self. Formalities and salary range Natural Sciences refers to the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Danish Universities under the Danish Ministry of Science, Technology and Innovation . The application must be in English and include a curriculum vitae, degree certificate, a complete list of publications, a statement of future research plans and information about research activities, teaching portfolio and verified information on previous teaching experience (if any). Guidelines for applicants can be found here. Appointment shall be in accordance with the collective labour agreement between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations. Further information on qualification requirements and job content may be found in the Memorandum on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Danish Universities . Salary and terms as agreed between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Confederation of Professional Unions at basic salary steps 4-8. Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. Research activities will be evaluated in relation to actual research time. Thus, we encourage applicants to specify periods of leave without research activities, in order to be able to subtract these periods from the span of the scientific career during the evaluation of scientific productivity. Aarhus University offers a broad variety of services for international researchers and accompanying families, including relocation service and career counselling to expat partners. Read more here . Please find more information about entering and working in Denmark here . Aarhus University also offers a Junior Researcher Development Programme targeted at career development for postdocs at AU. You can read more about it here . At the Faculty of Natural Science at Aarhus University, we strive to support our scientific staff in their career development. We focus on competency development and career clarification and want to make your opportunities transparent. On our website , you can find information on all types of scientific positions, as well as the entry criteria we use when assessing candidates. You can also read more about how we can assist you in your career planning and development. The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Anders Møller Professor, Deputy Head of Department, Department of Computer Science +4523309994 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Nat-Tech Administrative Centre - Nat-Tech HR +4520612514 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Tuesday 13 Oct 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/social-media-content-creator-department-of-computer-science": {
      "title": "Questions about the position ?",
      "description": "Social Media Content Creator, Department of Computer Science  - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Computer Science Social Media Content Creator, Department of Computer Science Deadline 15 Oct 23:59 CEST Expected start 15 Nov Department of Computer Science Åbogade 34 8200 Aarhus N Part-time position 5 hours per week ID: 169250 Apply Want to show what student life at the Department of Computer Science is really like – the good, the challenging and the fun? And do you know what makes content work for a student audience on Instagram? We are looking for a student to create authentic and engaging content for the Department of Computer Science’s Instagram channel, @csaudk . You will work closely with the department’s Communications Manager but will be expected to independently identify stories and create content from everyday student life, events and activities at the department. The position is from 15 November 2026, or as soon as possible thereafter. Your working hours will be 5 hours pr. week. What you will do plan, film and edit Reels about student life, events, courses, projects and people at the department create posts, memes and stories – from vox pops and interviews to behind-the-scenes content create content for and about current students, as well as content that helps recruit new students nationally and internationally create content showcasing student projects and research activities, communicating both student life and the academic work at the department cover student-related events and activities and give students an authentic insight into life at the department appear in front of the camera and act as a host when relevant identify stories and trends that are relevant to current and prospective students contribute ideas and inspiration to our social media planning We are looking for someone who is currently enrolled as a student has experience creating content specifically for social media can independently film and edit short-form video content such as Instagram Reels has experience with Canva or similar tools is comfortable approaching and interviewing fellow students and appearing on camera can work independently and take responsibility for developing an idea from concept to published content is fluent in English; Danish is an advantage but not a requirement It is an advantage if you already have experience creating social media content in a university, student organisation or similar environment. In your application, please include a current SOME-trend and explain how you would tailor it to the department’s channels. Place of work and area of employment The place of work is at Åbogade 34, 8200 Aarhus N, and the area of employment is Aarhus University with affiliated institutions. Questions For questions about the position, please contact Communications Manager Sofia H. Rasmussen at [email protected] or 24 42 43 45. Deadline All applications must be received no later than 15 October 2026. Formalities and salary range Employment is in accordance with the collective agreement for student teachers at universities etc., concluded between the Ministry of Taxation and the Student Trade Union (Studenteransattes Landsforbund) and the Danish Medical Students' Association (Foreningen af ​​Danske Lægestuderende). Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Sofia Hedegaard Rasmussen Communications Manager, Department of Computer Science - Secretariat +4524424345 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Nat-Tech Administrative Centre - Nat-Tech HR +4522228426 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Thursday 15 Oct 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/postdoctoral-position-for-the-project-human-ai-collaboration-imaginaries-interventions-interfaces": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral position for the project Human AI Collaboration: Imaginaries, Interventions, Interfaces",
      "description": "Postdoctoral position for the project Human AI Collaboration: Imaginaries, Interventions, Interfaces - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact School of Communication and Culture - Faculty: Arts Postdoctoral position for the project Human AI Collaboration: Imaginaries, Interventions, Interfaces Deadline 21 Oct 23:59 CEST Expected start 1 Jan School of Communication and Culture Langelandsgade 139 8000 Aarhus C Fixed term full-time position 1 Jan 2027 - 31 Dec 2027 ID: 169381 Apply The Department of Digital Design and Information Studies within the School of Communication and Culture at Aarhus University invites applications for a postdoctoral position “Human AI Collaboration: Imaginaries, Interventions, Interfaces” funded by Independent Research Fund Denmark – Culture and Communication. The postdoctoral researcher position is a full-time and 1 -year fixed-term position. The position begins on 01 January 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. The School of Communication and Culture is committed to diversity and encourages all qualified applicants to apply regardless of their personal background. Project The rapid development of Generative AI (GenAI) promises increased productivity but comes with a lack of transparency. HAIC-III offers an analytical, theoretical, and practical research perspective on GenAI as a cultural and creative interface, which includes artistic and design interventions. HAIC -III positions itself within the fields of electronic literature, critical data studies, and software studies, and it analyses how GenAI is interfaced (SP1), how GenAI creates new relations to archives (SP2), experiments with prototyping alternative interfaces to GenAI (SP3), and utilise artistic research to explore how AI affects contemporary imaginaries (SP4). How can we use artistic and design-based approaches to address and potentially mitigate problematic aspects of GenAI’s usage in cultural domains through a focus on creative human-AI collaboration? Rather than automation, HAIC-III's central focus is on human-AI collaboration and GenAI as cultural expression and creative interface. See the full project description here, including a detailed description of SPs and WPs: https://pure.au.dk/portal/da/projects/human-ai-collaboration-imaginaries-interventions-interfaces . Information about the project and its ongoing activities can be found here: https://darc.au.dk/projects/human-ai-collaboration-haic-iii Postdoctoral researcher position Your main tasks will consist of: contribute to the overall research project, with particular emphasis on SP5 (Human–AI Collaboration Lab) and the thematic WPs 1–3 (AI & Identity, AI & the Archive, and AI Interfaces); conduct research that contributes to one or more of the project’s subprojects: SP1 (Reading AI Platforms through Interface Criticism), SP2 (Generative Archives), SP3 (Prototyping Anti-mimetic AI), and/or SP4 (Crafting Collaborative Imaginaries); contribute to the effective implementation of the project and to its overall academic impact and outcomes, including research presentations, papers and journal articles; Teaching and supervision As a postdoctoral researcher, your position is primarily research-based, but it will also involve a small degree of teaching and supervision. To that end, the selected applicant will be expected to take part in the department’s teaching and supervision activities and to teach and supervise at BA and MA levels. The department has the following educations: Information Studies, Bachelor's Degree Programme in (2018) , Information Studies, Master's Degree Programme (2021) , Digital Design - IT, Aesthetics and Interaction, Bachelor's Degree Programme in (2024) and Digital Design, Master's Degree Programme in (2021) Given the international focus of the degree programmes, the chosen applicant will be expected to teach in English as well as Danish. Qualifications Applicants must have a PhD degree or must document equivalent qualifications in a relevant field related to digital design and aesthetics.  Applicants must be able to document, relevant to the position: an internationally oriented research profile within the field of digital design or similar relevant fields as documented by a PhD dissertation and/or relevant research publications experience in the professional management of research projects relevant teaching experience at university level as documented by a teaching portfolio (or equivalent documentation of teaching experience and qualifications) commensurate with the length of the applicant’s academic career excellent communication and interpersonal skills, in order to engage productively both within the research team and with external organisations and institutions. Furthermore, it will be considered an advantage if applicants can document: a demonstrated record of high-quality research publications recognized internationally, in line with the applicant’s career stage experience of participation in national and international research networks time spent abroad working at one or more internationally recognised research institutions. Finally, applicants are asked to provide a proposal for research to be undertaken within the stated framework of the research project (max. 1-2 pages). Please note that although the application process can be completed on the Aarhus University system without uploading publications or a teaching portfolio, applications that do not include uploaded publications (maximum two) will not be considered. Although the Aarhus University application system includes an option to upload letters of recommendation, please do not include letters of recommendation or references with the application. Applicants who are invited to an interview may be asked to provide references. Work environment Active participation in the department's daily life is a high priority, and we emphasise the importance of good working relationships, both among colleagues and with our students. In order to maintain and develop the department’s high-quality teaching and research environment, the selected applicant is expected to maintain a consistent, engaged presence within the department. We respect the balance between work and private life and aim to create a work environment in which that balance can be maintained. You can read more about family and work-life balance in Denmark. Aarhus University also offers a Junior Researcher Development Programme targeted at career development for postdoctoral researchers at AU. International applicants International applicants are encouraged to read about the attractive working conditions and other benefits of working at Aarhus University and in Denmark, including healthcare, paid holidays and, if relevant, maternity/paternity leave, childcare and schooling. Aarhus University offers a wide variety of services for international researchers and accompanying families, including a relocation service and an AU Expat Partner Programme . You can also find information about the taxation aspects of international researchers’ employment by AU . The department The place of employment is Department of Digital Design and Information Studies, Helsingforsgade 14, 8200 Aarhus N, Denmark Prospective applicants are invited to view the department’s website . School of Communication and Culture The school is a part of the Faculty of Arts. You will find information about the school and its research programmes , departments , and diverse activities on its website . Contact For further information about the position, please contact the principal investigator (PI), Søren Pold: [email protected] If you need help uploading your application or have questions about the recruitment process, please contact Arts HR support by email: [email protected] . Qualification requirements Applicants should hold a PhD or equivalent academic qualifications. Formalities Faculty of Arts refers to the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Danish Universities (the Appointment Order) . Further information on qualification requirements and job content may be found in the Memorandum on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Danish Universities . Further information on the application and supplementary materials may be found in Application Guidelines . The application must outline the applicant's motivation for applying for the position, attaching a curriculum vitae, a teaching portfolio, a complete list of published works, copies of degree certificates and examples of academic production ( mandatory, but no more than two examples ). Please upload this material electronically along with your application. Aarhus University also offers a junior researcher development programme targeted at career development for postdocs at AU. You can read more about it here: https://talent.au.dk/junior-researcher-development-programme/ If nothing else is noted, applications must be submitted in English. The application deadline is at 11.59 pm Danish time (same as Central European Time) on the deadline day. Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. Shortlists may be prepared with the candidates that have been selected for a detailed academic assessment. A committee set up by the head of school is responsible for selecting the most qualified candidates. See this link for further information about shortlisting at the Faculty of Arts: shortlisting Terms of employment Appointment shall be in accordance with the collective labour agreement between the Danish Ministry of Finance and the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations. Salary and terms of employment are governed by the Cirkulære om overenskomst for akademikere i staten (in Danish). You will be employed as a postdoc at base pay level 4–8 with additional supplements in accordance with the Cirkulære om protokollat om visse ansættelsesvilkår for videnskabeligt personale ved universiteter (in Danish). The job content and qualification requirements are described in further detail in the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of  Academic Staff at Universities . About Arts The Faculty of Arts is one of Northern Europe’s most significant faculties for research and higher education in the humanities, theology and education. Within this broad academic scope, the faculty comprises approximately 700 researchers, 200 PhD students, 9,000 Bachelor’s and Master’s degree students, and 1,500 further and continuing education students. We believe that the best ideas arise when different perspectives meet – and that research, teaching and innovation are best developed in dialogue with the surrounding society. You can find more information here: Faculty of Arts | Aarhus University The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website . Questions about the position\n                            ? Søren Pold Professor, School of Communication and Culture - Department of Digital Design and Information Studies +4587161994 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Arts Administrative Centre - Arts HR +4587162298 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Wednesday 21 Oct 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
